{"id":"mahabharata-1-197","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":197,"title":"सप्तनवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 197 · Vidura's counsel","summary":{"en":"Vidura tells Dhritarashtra that Bhishma and Drona speak for his good, that the Pandavas with Drupada, Krishna and the Vrishnis cannot be defeated, and that the people long to see them. He warns that Duryodhana's wrongdoing will destroy the people.","kn":"ಭೀಷ್ಮ ದ್ರೋಣರು ನಿನ್ನ ಹಿತಕ್ಕಾಗಿಯೇ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ, ದ್ರುಪದ, ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣ, ವೃಷ್ಣಿಗಳೊಂದಿಗಿರುವ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಸೋಲಿಸಲಾಗದು, ಪ್ರಜೆಗಳು ಅವರನ್ನು ಕಾಣಲು ಹಂಬಲಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ ಎಂದು ವಿದುರನು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಅಪರಾಧದಿಂದ ಪ್ರಜೆಗಳು ನಾಶವಾಗುವರೆಂದು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"विदुर धृतराष्ट्र से कहते हैं कि भीष्म और द्रोण उनके हित की बात कहते हैं, कि द्रुपद, श्रीकृष्ण और वृष्णियों सहित पाण्डव अजेय हैं, और प्रजा उन्हें देखने को लालायित है। वे चेतावनी देते हैं कि दुर्योधन के अपराध से प्रजा नष्ट होगी।","te":"భీష్మ ద్రోణులు నీ హితం కోసమే చెబుతున్నారని, ద్రుపదుడు, శ్రీకృష్ణుడు, వృష్ణులతో కూడిన పాండవులను ఓడించలేమని, ప్రజలు వారిని చూడాలని తహతహలాడుతున్నారని విదురుడు ధృతరాష్ట్రునికి చెబుతాడు. దుర్యోధనుని అపరాధం వల్ల ప్రజలు నశిస్తారని హెచ్చరిస్తాడు.","ta":"பீஷ்மரும் துரோணரும் உன் நன்மைக்காகவே சொல்கிறார்கள், த்ருபதன், ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர், வ்ருஷ்ணிகளுடன் இருக்கும் பாண்டவர்களை வெல்ல முடியாது, மக்கள் அவர்களைக் காண ஏங்குகிறார்கள் என்று விதுரர் திருதராஷ்டிரனிடம் சொல்கிறார். துரியோதனனின் குற்றத்தால் மக்கள் அழிவர் என்று எச்சரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ഭീഷ്മരും ദ്രോണരും തന്റെ നന്മയ്ക്കായാണ് സംസാരിക്കുന്നതെന്ന് വിദുരർ ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരോട് പറയുന്നു; ദ്രുപദനും കൃഷ്ണനും വൃഷ്ണികളും ചേർന്ന പാണ്ഡവരെ തോൽപ്പിക്കാനാവില്ലെന്നും, ജനങ്ങൾ അവരെ കാണാൻ ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നുവെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. ദുര്യോധനന്റെ തെറ്റായ പ്രവൃത്തികൾ ജനങ്ങളെ നശിപ്പിക്കുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.197; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"विदुरागमनपर्व","titleEn":"Viduragamana Parva (Vidura's coming)","verses":[{"text":"विदुर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vidura said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"राजन्निःसंशयं श्रेयो वाच्यस्त्वमसि बान्धवैः ।\nन त्वशुश्रूषमाणेषु वाक्यं संप्रतितिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, kinsmen are surely bound to tell you what is best for you; but advice finds no footing with those who refuse to listen."}},{"n":2,"text":"हितं हि तव तद्वाक्यमुक्तवान्कुरुसत्तमः ।\nभीष्मः शांतनवो राजन्प्रतिगृह्णासि तन्न च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, son of Shantanu and best of the Kurus, spoke to you what was truly good for you, O king, yet you do not accept it."}},{"n":3,"text":"तथा द्रोणेन बहुधा भाषितं हितमुत्तमम् ।\nतच्च राधासुतः कर्णो मन्यते न हितं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona too has urged excellent counsel for your good in many ways, but Karna, son of Radha, does not consider it good for you."}},{"n":4,"text":"चिन्तयंश्च न पश्यामि राजंस्तव सुहृत्तमम् ।\nआभ्यां पुरुषसिंहाभ्यां यो वा स्यात्प्रज्ञयाधिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"However I reflect, O king, I see no better friend to you than these two lions among men, or anyone wiser than they."}},{"n":5,"text":"इमौ हि वृद्धौ वयसा प्रज्ञया च श्रुतेन च ।\nसमौ च त्वयि राजेन्द्र तेषु पाण्डुसुतेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two are elders in age, in wisdom and in learning, and they hold you and the sons of Pandu in equal regard."}},{"n":6,"text":"धर्मे चानवमौ राजन्सत्यतायां च भारत ।\nरामाद्दाशरथेश्चैव गयाच्चैव न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In righteousness and truthfulness, O Bharata, they are second to none, not even to Rama son of Dasharatha or to Gaya; of that there is no doubt."}},{"n":7,"text":"न चोक्तवन्तावश्रेयः पुरस्तादपि किंचन ।\nन चाप्यपकृतं किंचिदनयोर्लक्ष्यते त्वयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"They have never given you harmful advice before, and no wrong done by them to you can be found."}},{"n":8,"text":"ताविमौ पुरुषव्याघ्रावनागसि नृप त्वयि ।\nन मन्त्रयेतां त्वच्छ्रेयः कथं सत्यपराक्रमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could these two tigers among men, devoted to truth and valor, advise anything against your good when you have done them no harm?"}},{"n":9,"text":"प्रज्ञावन्तौ नरश्रेष्ठावस्मिँल्लोके नराधिप ।\nत्वन्निमित्तमतो नेमौ किंचिज्जिह्मं वदिष्यतः ।\nइति मे नैष्ठिकी बुद्धिर्वर्तते कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are the wisest of men in this world, O king; for your sake they will not say anything crooked. This is my settled conviction, O joy of the Kurus."}},{"n":10,"text":"न चार्थहेतोर्धर्मज्ञौ वक्ष्यतः पक्षसंश्रितम् ।\nएतद्धि परमं श्रेयो मेनाते तव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing dharma, they will not speak out of partisanship or for gain; they consider this the highest good for you, O Bharata."}},{"n":11,"text":"दुर्योधनप्रभृतयः पुत्रा राजन्यथा तव ।\nतथैव पाण्डवेयास्ते पुत्रा राजन्न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just as Duryodhana and the rest are your sons, O king, so beyond doubt are the Pandavas."}},{"n":12,"text":"तेषु चेदहितं किंचिन्मन्त्रयेयुरबुद्धितः ।\nमन्त्रिणस्ते न ते श्रेयः प्रपश्यन्ति विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If your counselors were to plan some harm to them out of folly, then they do not truly see your good."}},{"n":13,"text":"अथ ते हृदये राजन्विशेषस्तेषु वर्तते ।\nअन्तरस्थं विवृण्वानाः श्रेयः कुर्युर्न ते ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And if in your heart you favor one side over the other, then by revealing that hidden leaning they would surely not serve your good either."}},{"n":14,"text":"एतदर्थमिमौ राजन्महात्मानौ महाद्युती ।\nनोचतुर्विवृतं किंचिन्न ह्येष तव निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this reason, O king, these two great and radiant men have not spoken openly, for this is not your real resolve."}},{"n":15,"text":"यच्चाप्यशक्यतां तेषामाहतुः पुरुषर्षभौ ।\nतत्तथा पुरुषव्याघ्र तव तद्भद्रमस्तु ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"And whatever those two bulls among men said about the Pandavas being unconquerable, it is so, O tiger among men; may it bring you welfare."}},{"n":16,"text":"कथं हि पाण्डवः श्रीमान्सव्यसाची परंतपः ।\nशक्यो विजेतुं संग्रामे राजन्मघवता अपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could the glorious Pandava Arjuna, the left-handed archer, scourge of foes, be defeated in battle, even by Indra himself?"}},{"n":17,"text":"भीमसेनो महाबाहुर्नागायुतबलो महान् ।\nकथं हि युधि शक्येत विजेतुममरैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could mighty Bhimasena of long arms, with the strength of ten thousand elephants, be conquered in battle even by the immortals?"}},{"n":18,"text":"तथैव कृतिनौ युद्धे यमौ यमसुताविव ।\nकथं विषहितुं शक्यौ रणे जीवितुमिच्छता ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too the twins, skilled in war like the two sons of Yama; how could anyone who wishes to live withstand them in combat?"}},{"n":19,"text":"यस्मिन्धृतिरनुक्रोशः क्षमा सत्यं पराक्रमः ।\nनित्यानि पाण्डवश्रेष्ठे स जीयेत कथं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could he be defeated in battle in whom steadiness, compassion, forbearance, truth and valor ever dwell, the best of the Pandavas?"}},{"n":20,"text":"येषां पक्षधरो रामो येषां मन्त्री जनार्दनः ।\nकिं नु तैरजितं संख्ये येषां पक्षे च सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What have those not conquered in war who have Rama as their supporter, Janardana as their counselor, and Satyaki on their side?"}},{"n":21,"text":"द्रुपदः श्वशुरो येषां येषां श्यालाश्च पार्षताः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नमुखा वीरा भ्रातरो द्रुपदात्मजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their father-in-law is Drupada, their brothers-in-law are the Parshatas, and the heroic sons of Drupada led by Dhrishtadyumna are their kin."}},{"n":22,"text":"सोऽशक्यतां च विज्ञाय तेषामग्रेण भारत ।\nदायाद्यतां च धर्मेण सम्यक्तेषु समाचर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing then, O Bharata, that they are unconquerable, and that they have a rightful claim to inheritance, deal with them properly."}},{"n":23,"text":"इदं निर्दिग्धमयशः पुरोचनकृतं महत् ।\nतेषामनुग्रहेणाद्य राजन्प्रक्षालयात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great infamy, blackened by what Purochana did, you can wash from yourself today, O king, by showing them favor."}},{"n":24,"text":"द्रुपदोऽपि महान्राजा कृतवैरश्च नः पुरा ।\nतस्य संग्रहणं राजन्स्वपक्षस्य विवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Drupada is also powerful and was once our enemy; winning him over, O king, would strengthen your own side."}},{"n":25,"text":"बलवन्तश्च दाशार्हा बहवश्च विशां पते ।\nयतः कृष्णस्ततस्ते स्युर्यतः कृष्णस्ततो जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Dasharhas are mighty and many, O lord of the people; where Krishna is, they will be, and where Krishna is, there is victory."}},{"n":26,"text":"यच्च साम्नैव शक्येत कार्यं साधयितुं नृप ।\nको दैवशप्तस्तत्कार्तुं विग्रहेण समाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a task can be accomplished by conciliation alone, O king, who, unless cursed by fate, would choose to do it by strife?"}},{"n":27,"text":"श्रुत्वा च जीवतः पार्थान्पौरजानपदो जनः ।\nबलवद्दर्शने गृध्नुस्तेषां राजन्कुरु प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard that the Parthas live, the townsfolk and country people are eager to see them; do what pleases them, O king."}},{"n":28,"text":"दुर्योधनश्च कर्णश्च शकुनिश्चापि सौबलः ।\nअधर्मयुक्ता दुष्प्रज्ञा बाला मैषां वचः कृथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, Karna and Shakuni son of Subala are unrighteous, foolish and childish; do not follow their words."}},{"n":29,"text":"उक्तमेतन्मया राजन्पुरा गुणवतस्तव ।\nदुर्योधनापराधेन प्रजेयं विनशिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"I told you this earlier, O king, when you were virtuous: through Duryodhana's offense these people will perish."}}]}]}